    "findings": [
      "M1-vs-reference: RMS3D 1346.5 km dominated by a 690.0 km/day transverse drift (constant mean-motion mismatch of the purely-Keplerian model: the mean-vs-osculating a offset at the initialization epoch plus absent J2 secular rates); adding J2 removes skill 0.9933 of the residual (CI [0.9933, 0.9979]) -> improvement-exceeds-CI-and-envelope.",
      "M3(primary beta=100) WORSENS agreement vs M2: skill -2.2794 (CI [-6.4246, -2.3192], excludes zero on the negative side) -> worse-than-previous-model. Reported verbatim per anti-overfitting doctrine; no atmospheric or beta parameter was retuned.",
      "[INFERENCE] The beta band responds monotonically (transverse trend c1: {\"beta50\": 43.64, \"beta100\": 18.24, \"beta200\": 5.57, \"beta400\": -0.76} km/day), crossing zero only at the band edge (beta=400 -> RMS3D 3.13 km). The drag signature is detectable, but the compatible effective beta lies AT OR BEYOND the pre-declared band edge; extending the band or picking the nicest member post hoc would be tuning and is deliberately not done. Any refined-beta study must be a separately declared experiment.",
      "[INFERENCE] M2's leftover secular drift (-7.08 km/day; -5.89 km/day under SGP4-heritage GM) implies the reference mean semilatus evolves as if decaying at -40.3 m/day relative to our non-decaying model (consistent with TLE-B*-absorbed drag plus density-weather; not independently separable).",
      "SGP4-heritage-GM sensitivity shifts M2 RMS3D by -1.605 km (constants/convention term bounded, canon retained).",
      "Integration bound (NSUB 16 vs 8): 19.6 m (self-convergence order p = 4.93); reference-interpolation diagnostic bounded by 5.80e+01 km at worst subsampled cadence and never enters headline numbers (exact-grid alignment). Contamination gate: no sample exceeded the 100 m second-difference threshold (max 41.7 m)."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Reference is TLE/SGP4-provenance (disclosed in the object sheet); its own error grows ~1-3 km/day from the revision date per JPL documentation, so residuals measure model-vs-reference divergence jointly with reference uncertainty (never separated).",
      "Constant-beta drag with a static exponential atmosphere idealizes ISS attitude-dependent area and thermospheric weather; no drag-improvement claim is made unless it exceeds both the bootstrap CI and the declared envelope (decision rule applied automatically).",
      "Unmodelled physics remaining: lunisolar third-body, tesseral/zonal harmonics beyond J2, SRP, relativity -- jointly attributed with reference uncertainty to the remainder.",
      "TEME->ICRF conversion inside Horizons is undocumented; its effect is inseparable from the reference's own solution and therefore part of the remainder.",
